{"callables":[],"check_receipt":{"codes":[],"sha256":"8868a5d3c354ba6603247edc628ca6bb5de44cd76be1206c9fc0b7f9c685ff1b","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c","verdict":"CURRENT_CHECKED","verifier_sha256":"33beb7ab3efda75ecf5cada95ee97b7ff74269abbf6d8c387831f6bca8f207e6"},"constructs":["infer","inputs","model","outputs","permits"],"corpus":"nika-pack-foundation@34ad76c5376a","exposure":"EXPOSED","facets":{},"file":"examples/pack-10-compose-child.nika","file_sha256":"8868a5d3c354ba6603247edc628ca6bb5de44cd76be1206c9fc0b7f9c685ff1b","id":"example:pack:10-compose-child","intent":"Compose (the child) — a callable unit. The second half of lesson 10: a workflow written to be CALLED. Its `inputs:` are the parameters a parent may pass, its typed `outputs:` are the whole surface a parent can read — nothing else crosses the wall. Read `10-compose-pipeline.nika` first; it invokes this file.","kind":"example","language":"en","pin":{"binary":"nika 0.123.0-preview.1 (90d2472cd)","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c"},"proof_level":"CHECKED","provenance":{"activity":"foundry.spec.pack_examples","created_at":"2026-10-11T22:18:28Z","model":null,"sources":["src:pack:90d2472cd"]},"sha256":"96daef865a26f4c0a5e9bf512cef06912cff52e73db24678d79291232ae0d5f0","split":"DEV","status":"EXAMPLE","title":"Compose (the child) — a callable unit.","topology":"linear","trust":"imported"}
{"callables":["nika:jq"],"check_receipt":{"codes":[],"sha256":"697f2dc80c321eb7c90329f6be6ce76acbcad47d69bcba5da7b6108d131ccca7","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c","verdict":"CURRENT_CHECKED","verifier_sha256":"33beb7ab3efda75ecf5cada95ee97b7ff74269abbf6d8c387831f6bca8f207e6"},"constructs":["inputs","invoke","invoke.tool","invoke.workflow","model","outputs","permits","permits.tools","returns","with"],"corpus":"nika-pack-foundation@34ad76c5376a","exposure":"EXPOSED","facets":{},"file":"examples/pack-10-compose-pipeline.nika","file_sha256":"697f2dc80c321eb7c90329f6be6ce76acbcad47d69bcba5da7b6108d131ccca7","id":"example:pack:10-compose-pipeline","intent":"Compose — one workflow calls another. Anything non-trivial is built from parts, and this is the door: a task whose `invoke:` names a `workflow:` instead of a `tool:`. The target is a STATIC path (never `${{ }}` · `NIKA-COMP-001`), resolved relative to THIS file; `args:` feed the child's declared `inputs:`; the task's `.output` is the closed object of the child's `outputs:` — the wall between the two files is the child's signature, nothing more.","kind":"example","language":"en","pin":{"binary":"nika 0.123.0-preview.1 (90d2472cd)","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c"},"proof_level":"CHECKED","provenance":{"activity":"foundry.spec.pack_examples","created_at":"2026-10-11T22:18:28Z","model":null,"sources":["src:pack:90d2472cd"]},"sha256":"a32b3f8f8e392a770fe1cf384e0fffb72b5652bbe1b51fcf6d6c28af8eda4977","split":"DEV","status":"EXAMPLE","title":"Compose — one workflow calls another.","topology":"subworkflow","trust":"imported"}
{"callables":["nika:jq","nika:read"],"check_receipt":{"codes":[],"sha256":"3fae0c973a8bf84abce8746f8cc140bc012c4f8d48df8b932da6395c6eaa6430","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c","verdict":"CURRENT_CHECKED","verifier_sha256":"33beb7ab3efda75ecf5cada95ee97b7ff74269abbf6d8c387831f6bca8f207e6"},"constructs":["inputs","invoke","invoke.tool","lift","lift.taint","outputs","permits","permits.fs","permits.tools","with"],"corpus":"nika-pack-foundation@34ad76c5376a","exposure":"EXPOSED","facets":{},"file":"examples/pack-11-lift-the-door.nika","file_sha256":"3fae0c973a8bf84abce8746f8cc140bc012c4f8d48df8b932da6395c6eaa6430","id":"example:pack:11-lift-the-door","intent":"The lift — the one door through the taint. A permit-relevant argument fed by an UNTRUSTED value (`inputs.*` · anything fetched) is the parameterisation taint. When the check can resolve the value and it ESCAPES the bound, it refuses with `NIKA-AUTH-008` — and the reflex that refusal provokes (widen the boundary until the message stops) is the wrong door. The right one is authored: a `lift:` entry naming the **taint** law on the task, with a reviewable `because:` (spec/10-authority.md · \"The only door is the authored one\").","kind":"example","language":"en","pin":{"binary":"nika 0.123.0-preview.1 (90d2472cd)","spec_sha":"34ad76c5376ab6b1fb02e3e4c455ff23f1c1312c"},"proof_level":"CHECKED","provenance":{"activity":"foundry.spec.pack_examples","created_at":"2026-10-11T22:18:28Z","model":null,"sources":["src:pack:90d2472cd"]},"sha256":"d48168ebef0722f5764640dbe16ddd3d1b32abd99a732427ec614cc4c37308e3","split":"DEV","status":"EXAMPLE","title":"The lift — the one door through the taint.","topology":"linear","trust":"imported"}
